 "panels": [
  {
   "type": "text",
   "title": "",
   "transparent": true,
   "options": {
    "mode": "markdown",
    "content": "**Is the DEX turning offered load into cleared trades?** The load generator's offered operations (per second, by op) should be met by placed and cleared orders; its errors and busy replies are load the DEX turned away. The headline is the soak's verdict (PASS \u2265 0.9999): of the orders that could trade, the share that did, counting an order stuck open (silent 10 min) as a miss. The DEX's own live figure counts only orders that reached an end, so it reads 1.0 while a backlog builds: watch **Orders open too long** beside it."
   },
   "id": 1,
   "gridPos": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 0,
    "w": 24,
    "h": 3
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "stat",
   "title": "Clearing SLO (soak verdict) \u00b7 PASS \u2265 0.9999",
   "description": "The soak's verdict (offchain/soak_verdict.py, pushed at the end of a soak): cleared \u00f7 (cleared + missed + stuck open) over the orders that could trade; an order with no end and no event for 10 min is stuck open. Empty until a soak of this run has judged it. Read as pushed by the range's end (a verdict comes at, or after, the run's end).",
   "datasource": {
    "type": "prometheus",
    "uid": "prometheus"
   },
   "targets": [
    {
     "expr": "max(soak_check_value{run_id=\"$run_id\",check=\"clearing_slo\"})",
     "refId": "A",
     "range": false,
     "instant": true
    }
   ],
   "fieldConfig": {
    "defaults": {
     "decimals": 4,
     "noValue": "no verdict yet",
     "color": {
      "mode": "thresholds"
     },
     "thresholds": {
      "mode": "absolute",
      "steps": [
       {
        "color": "red",
        "value": null
       },
       {
        "color": "green",
        "value": 0.9999
       }
      ]
     },
     "unit": "percentunit"
    },
    "overrides": []
   },
   "options": {
    "graphMode": "none",
    "colorMode": "background",
    "textMode": "value",
    "justifyMode": "center",
    "reduceOptions": {
     "calcs": [
      "lastNotNull"
     ],
     "fields": "",
     "values": false
    }
   },
   "id": 2,
   "gridPos": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 3,
    "w": 4,
    "h": 4
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "stat",
   "title": "Cleared of settled orders (live, info)",
   "description": "The DEX's running tally (offchain/order_telemetry.py): filled \u00f7 (filled + expired, lost, rejected, partially cancelled) over marketable orders that reached an end. An order that never reaches one is not in it, so a backlog leaves it at 1.0; the verdict counts those (Orders open too long).",
   "datasource": {
    "type": "prometheus",
    "uid": "prometheus"
   },
   "targets": [
    {
     "expr": "last_over_time((min(jamswap_order_clearing_slo{net=\"$net\",run_id=\"$run_id\"}))[$__range:$__interval] @ $at)",
     "refId": "A",
     "range": false,
     "instant": true
    }
   ],
   "fieldConfig": {
    "defaults": {
     "decimals": 4,
     "noValue": "no data",
     "color": {
      "mode": "fixed",
      "fixedColor": "text"
     },
     "unit": "percentunit"
    },
    "overrides": []
   },
   "options": {
    "graphMode": "none",
    "colorMode": "background",
    "textMode": "value",
    "justifyMode": "center",
    "reduceOptions": {
     "calcs": [
      "lastNotNull"
     ],
     "fields": "",
     "values": false
    }
   },
   "id": 3,
   "gridPos": {
    "x": 4,
    "y": 3,
    "w": 4,
    "h": 4
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "stat",
   "title": "Orders open too long \u00b7 PASS = 0",
   "description": "Live orders with no event for 10 min (resting ones: 10 min past their own expiry): what the verdict will count as stuck open, as it builds (jamswap_order_open_stale).",
   "datasource": {
    "type": "prometheus",
    "uid": "prometheus"
   },
   "targets": [
    {
     "expr": "last_over_time((sum(jamswap_order_open_stale{net=\"$net\",run_id=\"$run_id\"}))[$__range:$__interval] @ $at)",
     "refId": "A",
     "range": false,
     "instant": true
    }
   ],
   "fieldConfig": {
    "defaults": {
     "decimals": 0,
     "noValue": "no data",
